-- title:
--   OAI.Saxl.Balance.short_pair_support: intermediate lemma from OpenAI, Universal Tensor Squares for Symmetric Groups (result family 205)
-- statement:
--   An intermediate lemma of the split of OpenAI's proof of `OAI.UniversalTensorSquares.universal_tensor_square`, carved from OpenAI's openai/math development for this platform. The statement and its proof are OpenAI's (OpenAI, *Universal Tensor Squares for Symmetric Groups (result family 205)*, OpenAI Math Release, September 24, 2026, result family 205, [github.com/openai/math](https://github.com/openai/math), Apache License 2.0); in Lean it is the declaration `OAI.Saxl.Balance.short_pair_support` of [lean/OAI/RepresentationTheory/UniversalSquare/Specht/FinitePieri.lean](https://github.com/openai/math/blob/7ef5c0cc5ca4b0e072b7a050fca09ab24bc6fa3a/lean/OAI/RepresentationTheory/UniversalSquare/Specht/FinitePieri.lean) at commit 7ef5c0c, ported to Lean 4.33.1 and Mathlib 0df444a.
--
--   **The statement**, as published (namespace `OAI.Saxl.Balance`, with `open scoped TensorProduct`, `open FlagColumns Columns`):
--
--   ```lean
--   lemma short_pair_support {n : ℕ} (q δ : ℕ) (hn : n = 2*q+δ)
--       (hδ : δ = 1 ∨ δ = 2)
--       (a : Tableau n (ShortColumns.shape q δ).transpose)
--       (μ : YoungDiagram) (t : Tableau n μ) (hμ : μ.colLen 0 ≤ 4)
--       (ho : δ = 2 → ∃ j, μ.colLen j % 2 = 1) :
--       ∃ F : Representation.IntertwiningMap (spechtRep t)
--         (projectedSpechtTensor a a (inOutputs (Set.Icc q (pairUpper q δ)))
--           (inOutputs_invariant (Set.Icc q (pairUpper q δ)))).toRepresentation, F ≠ 0
--   ```
--
